MISSION_TITLE=
Epoch 3 closure · Mission Control lifecycle database · historical compatibility · Epoch 4 scaffold

MISSION_OBJECTIVE=
Close the remaining Mission Control and control-database architectural gap before Epoch 4: eliminate historical mission HTTP 404 failures; represent schema-era absence truthfully; make refresh, audit, restart, component-start contract, add-component, redesign and rollback planning explicit; preserve exact authority/effect separation; finish or supersede the active Epoch 3 mission chain; restore the LPCL Panel as a live integrated control surface; validate the exact repository candidate and GitHub state; and produce the reconciled Epoch 4 handoff without promoting future Semantic Inference Compiler target architecture to AS-IS.

MISSION_DESCRIPTION=
This is a successor closure mission for the end of Epoch 3. It extends the already-authorized hybrid Local plus ChatGPT SaaS control-plane recovery with a versioned Mission Control database lifecycle, historical-schema compatibility and mission redesign scaffolding. Historical evidence must never be rewritten into fabricated modern process state. Material effects are allowed only through exact bounded adapters already proven for the relevant mission; unsupported component/restart/rollback actions fail closed into typed revision or plan state. Database migrations are additive, versioned, auditable and rollback-aware. The mission must leave LION MISSION CONTROL and LION CONTROL LPCL PANEL as the operational entry surfaces for Epoch 4, while repository validation remains the proof boundary.

